 {slug:'interior-plastering',title:'Interior plastering',short:'Get the foundations of your room right.',image:'hero',intro:'From a single room to a larger renovation, get the interior surfaces ready for the space you have in mind.',body:'A beautiful interior begins before the paint goes on. Lyons Interiors provides residential interior plastering and surface preparation, with the scope based on the condition of the property rather than a one-size-fits-all package. Share the room, the stage of your project and the result you are working towards.',items:['Residential walls and interior surfaces','Surface preparation for renovation projects','Plastering coordinated with your refurbishment plans'],expect:'We discuss the surfaces, access and sequence of work, then identify the preparation and finishing required. Your quote should make the agreed work and any exclusions clear before a booking is arranged.',not:'Painting, electrical work and other trades are not automatically included in a plastering quote. Agree responsibilities before work starts.',guide:'plastering-cost-leeds'},
 {slug:'ceilings',title:'Ceiling plastering',short:'Look up. Love what you see.',image:'bedroom',intro:'A smooth ceiling can bring a whole room together. Start with a conversation about its condition and the finish you would like.',body:'Ceilings deserve the same consideration as walls. Existing coatings, access, the stability of the background and any signs of leaks all affect the appropriate approach. Send a clear photograph of the whole ceiling, plus close-ups of any problem areas, without disturbing the surface.',items:['Ceiling resurfacing where the background is suitable','Finishing ceilings as part of a room renovation','Advice on preparation and the next steps'],expect:'We first need to understand what the ceiling is made of and what is already on it. Any suspected asbestos-containing coating must be assessed before work that could disturb it is planned.',not:'Do not scrape, sand or drill a suspect textured ceiling to prepare for a quote. Specialist assessment may be required. Asbestos removal is not offered on this website.',guide:'textured-ceilings-and-asbestos'},
 {slug:'plaster-repairs',title:'Plaster repairs',short:'Small problem. Proper attention.',image:'detail',intro:'Not every damaged wall needs starting again. Find out whether a local repair or a wider finish makes more sense.',body:'Damage left after other trades, isolated failed areas and old patchwork all deserve a considered approach. The aim is to choose a repair that suits the surrounding surface and your decorating plans, rather than automatically recommending the largest job.',items:['Localised damaged plaster and making-good work','Finishing around areas affected by renovation','Advice on patch repairs versus a full-wall skim'],expect:'Show us the size of the damaged area and a wider view of the wall. Explain what caused the damage and whether the problem is still active. The condition of the surrounding plaster matters as much as the visible patch.',not:'A cosmetic repair should not hide unresolved water ingress or continuing movement. If cracks are changing or accompanied by other building movement, seek a competent building assessment.',guide:'patch-repair-or-reskim'},
 {slug:'refurbishment-finishing',title:'Refurbishment finishing',short:'Bring the whole project together.',image:'kitchen',intro:'Turn the building-work stage into surfaces ready for the next chapter of your home.',body:'Refurbishment brings decisions, different trades and plenty of moving parts. Interior preparation and plastering need to fit the project sequence. Lyons Interiors helps with the finishing stage so that walls and ceilings are considered as part of the whole space, not isolated jobs.',items:['Interior surface preparation during refurbishment','Plastering across multiple rooms or project stages','Finishing after agreed preparatory work by other trades'],expect:'Share plans or room photographs, the stage of your refurbishment and the other trades involved. We discuss access, what needs completing first and where plastering fits before a working sequence is agreed.',not:'The service is interior preparation and plastering, not a claim to provide every trade or act as the main contractor. Confirm the exact responsibilities in your quote.',guide:'planning-your-plastering-project'},
 {slug:'commercial-plastering',title:'Commercial plastering',short:'A better finish for your business.',image:'studio',intro:'Professional interior plastering and finishing for commercial spaces in Leeds and West Yorkshire.',body:'Your space needs to work for the people using it. Whether you are refreshing a room or coordinating a broader refurbishment, explain the operating hours, access restrictions and other contractors involved so the plastering scope can be considered properly.',items:['Interior plastering for commercial premises','Preparation and finishing during refurbishment','Project enquiries from property owners and contractors'],expect:'Include plans where available, the intended use of the space and the proposed programme. Any project-specific specifications, fire or acoustic requirements, and site documentation need to be discussed and confirmed rather than assumed.',not:'Specialist performance, certification, out-of-hours working and completion dates are not promised without reviewing the project. Get requirements agreed in writing.',guide:'commercial-plastering-checklist'}
